OL,3,GNEWSARichard Rogers' home given to
OL,4,ANational Trust
OL,5,
OL,6,FThe family home of the celebrated
OL,7,Farchitect behind the Lloyd's building
OL,8,Fand the Pompidou Centre has been
OL,9,Fdonated to the National Trust.
OL,11,FRichard Rogers' home in Wimbledon,
OL,12,Fsouth-west London, known as the Rogers
OL,13,FHouse, was built in 1968 and has become
OL,14,Fa landmark in its own right.
OL,16,FThe property, 22 Parkside, was designed
OL,17,Fby Rogers and his first wife Su Rogers,
OL,18,Falso an architect. Lord Rogers died in
OL,19,F2021 aged 88.
OL,23,APub: 11-SepQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
OL,24,ANext PageBLon/SE NewsCReg TVFClean Feed
